{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungLatticeCornerCount"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded.lexGtOn_induction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded.lexGtOn_induction","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLexWellFounded.lean#L69-L77","doc":"Recursion along the lex order, in the form an induction on shapes actually uses:\nto prove `C μ` for every shape of size `n`, it suffices to prove it for `μ` given it for\nevery **lex-greater** shape of the same size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded.instIsWellFoundedLexGtOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded.instIsWellFoundedLexGtOn","kind":"instance","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLexWellFounded.lean#L66-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded.lexGtOn_wellFounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded.lexGtOn_wellFounded","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLexWellFounded.lean#L61-L64","doc":"**The outer induction of Mathas 3.14 is well-founded.**  A strict order on a finite\ntype is well-founded, and shapes of a fixed size are finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLexWellFounded.instIsTransLexG